      </connector>
      <label>Partner</label>
    </rules>
  </decisions>
  <description
  >Template for the automation "Keep both sides of relationships in step" (registry row Relationship_Reciprocal). Save As a new flow, change your copy, activate it, then switch ours off on the Automation page of BarnCRM Settings. Copy the delete template too. Writes the other side of every relationship whose Keep Both Sides In Step box is ticked, pairs it with a matching other side already on file instead of duplicating it, and keeps the other side's people, type, status, dates, and description equal to the side that was edited. A flow cannot run on a restore from the recycle bin, and this one does not read the Keep both sides setting. Your copy does not read our switch or the pause: activating it is its switch. See the admin guide page flow-templates.md.</description>
  <environments>Default</environments>
  <formulas>
    <description>The person on this side, whether held as a contact or as an account.</description>
    <name>fFromId</name>
    <dataType>String</dataType>
    <expression>BLANKVALUE({!$Record.Contact__c}, {!$Record.Person_Account__c})</expression>
  </formulas>
  <formulas>
    <description>The status the other side carries: this side's, or Current when it has none.</description>
    <name>fMirrorStatus</name>
    <dataType>String</dataType>
    <expression>IF(ISBLANK(TEXT({!$Record.Status__c})), "Current", TEXT({!$Record.Status__c}))</expression>
  </formulas>
  <formulas>
    <description>The type the other side takes: the mapped type, or Other when the type has no mapping.</description>
    <name>fReciprocalType</name>
    <dataType>String</dataType>
    <expression>BLANKVALUE({!varMappedType}, "Other")</expression>
  </formulas>
  <formulas>
    <description>The person on the other side, whether held as a contact or as an account.</description>
    <name>fToId</name>
    <dataType>String</dataType>
    <expression>BLANKVALUE({!$Record.Related_Contact__c}, {!$Record.Related_Person_Account__c})</expression>
  </formulas>
  <interviewLabel>BarnCRM template: Keep both sides of relationships in step {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
  <isTemplate>true</isTemplate>
  <label>BarnCRM template: Keep both sides of relationships in step</label>
